NAME
       brk, sbrk - change the data segment size

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int   brk(void *addr);
       void *sbrk(intptr_t increment);

DESCRIPTION
       Moves the top of the heap. Pages are mapped as the break grows
       and unmapped as it shrinks.

       These are the foundation malloc is built on; call malloc rather
       than these unless you are writing an allocator.

RETURN VALUE
       sbrk returns the previous break, or (void *)-1 on failure. brk
       returns the current break.

ERRORS
       ENOMEM   no memory, or the request is outside the allowed range

SEE ALSO
       mmap(2), malloc(3)
